This article presents a summary of my final work [1] for the
master's degree course in Mathematics, presented on November 1, 2018.
This work shows an introduction to the basic commands of the MetaPost
language. For this, some mathematical concepts are explained, as they
are part of its programming. It is shown how these concepts can be used
to create high-quality figures used in areas of mathematics such as
geometry and the study of graphs of real functions.
